      "text": "1. Project Story — Model Foundry",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Project Story — Model Foundry",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "id7598244",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 36.16015625,
      "y": -101.21875,
      "width": 548.6937255859375,
      "height": 405,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 9055640,
      "version": 40,
      "versionNonce": 2001222731,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784078163463,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Context\n• Model owners used multiple tools for health, freshness,\n  ownership, lineage, compliance, and inference activity.\n• Data came from Quasar, PyTorch, Venice, HDFS, Openhouse,\n  Ambry, MySQL, Hive, and monitoring pipelines.\n\nProblem\n• Slow page loads, fragmented workflows, inconsistent health\n  semantics, stale/partial data, and poor debuggability.\n\nMy role\n• Drove information architecture, FE contracts, performance,\n  shared components, rollout, and cross-team alignment.\n\nStaff framing\n• Not “I built a dashboard.”\n• “I created a trustworthy decision system and reusable\n  frontend foundations for multiple product surfaces.”",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Context\n• Model owners used multiple tools for health, freshness,\n  ownership, lineage, compliance, and inference activity.\n• Data came from Quasar, PyTorch, Venice, HDFS, Openhouse,\n  Ambry, MySQL, Hive, and monitoring pipelines.\n\nProblem\n• Slow page loads, fragmented workflows, inconsistent health\n  semantics, stale/partial data, and poor debuggability.\n\nMy role\n• Drove information architecture, FE contracts, performance,\n  shared components, rollout, and cross-team alignment.\n\nStaff framing\n• Not “I built a dashboard.”\n• “I created a trustworthy decision system and reusable\n  frontend foundations for multiple product surfaces.”",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
