      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6. Rendering Thousands of Chart Points",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6. Rendering Thousands of Chart Points",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "id1470156",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2493.765625,
      "y": 459.1875,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 446.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1f2937",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 3691718,
      "version": 114,
      "versionNonce": 320064549,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784077449200,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Data strategy\n• Aggregate server-side by viewport and time range\n• Return min/max/avg buckets instead of raw events\n• Downsample with LTTB or reservoir sampling\n• Use cursor/window APIs for historical data\n• Compress payloads and omit unused metadata\n\nRendering strategy\n• Canvas/WebGL for thousands of points\n• SVG for smaller interactive datasets\n• Memoize scales and transformed series\n• Avoid rebuilding chart objects on every render\n• Move expensive transforms to Web Worker\n• Render summary first, chart second\n• Use IntersectionObserver for below-the-fold charts\n• ResizeObserver + requestAnimationFrame for responsive layout\n\nUX strategy\n• Show summary, trend, latest value, and freshness first\n• Provide accessible table/download for chart data\n• Distinguish loading, stale, empty, and partial states",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Data strategy\n• Aggregate server-side by viewport and time range\n• Return min/max/avg buckets instead of raw events\n• Downsample with LTTB or reservoir sampling\n• Use cursor/window APIs for historical data\n• Compress payloads and omit unused metadata\n\nRendering strategy\n• Canvas/WebGL for thousands of points\n• SVG for smaller interactive datasets\n• Memoize scales and transformed series\n• Avoid rebuilding chart objects on every render\n• Move expensive transforms to Web Worker\n• Render summary first, chart second\n• Use IntersectionObserver for below-the-fold charts\n• ResizeObserver + requestAnimationFrame for responsive layout\n\nUX strategy\n• Show summary, trend, latest value, and freshness first\n• Provide accessible table/download for chart data\n• Distinguish loading, stale, empty, and partial states",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
