      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 2053079435,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1784077983659,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Clarify in interview\n• React Virtual DOM reduces manual DOM mutations,\n  but it does not make huge trees free.\n• Reconciliation still costs CPU.\n• Browser layout, paint, and memory remain bottlenecks.\n\nFor large tables\n• Prefer pagination for accessibility and simpler workflows\n• Use virtualization for thousands of interactive rows\n• Stable keys, overscan, fixed/estimated row height\n• Memoize row boundaries only after profiling\n• Keep callbacks and row props stable\n• Avoid rendering hidden columns\n• Move filtering/sorting server-side at high scale\n\nTrade-offs\n• Browser find, screen readers, printing, and focus handling\n  become harder with virtualization.",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Clarify in interview\n• React Virtual DOM reduces manual DOM mutations,\n  but it does not make huge trees free.\n• Reconciliation still costs CPU.\n• Browser layout, paint, and memory remain bottlenecks.\n\nFor large tables\n• Prefer pagination for accessibility and simpler workflows\n• Use virtualization for thousands of interactive rows\n• Stable keys, overscan, fixed/estimated row height\n• Memoize row boundaries only after profiling\n• Keep callbacks and row props stable\n• Avoid rendering hidden columns\n• Move filtering/sorting server-side at high scale\n\nTrade-offs\n• Browser find, screen readers, printing, and focus handling\n  become harder with virtualization.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
